---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { baseUrl } from '../../utils/base.ts';
---

<Layout
  title="Try UOMP via Aegis OS"
  description="aegis-os memory setup imports notes, writes the client config, and starts the background server. The first request comes from the agent, and Aegis OS opens the local consent page automatically."
  lang="en"
  switchHref={`${baseUrl}try/`}
>
  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <h1 style="margin-bottom:.25rem">Try UOMP via Aegis OS</h1>
      <p style="color:var(--mid);max-width:620px;line-height:1.65">
        Today one <code>aegis-os memory setup</code> command imports Markdown notes, starts the background server, and writes the Claude Desktop / Cursor / OpenCode config. It does not pre-authorize anything. UOMP is the memory module of Aegis OS; consent, leases, and audit are enforced by Aegis.
        When you ask the client for notes, the MCP bridge creates a consent request; Aegis OS opens the local trusted consent UI automatically, and the agent continues after you select the scope. No second terminal is required; the CLI remains a fallback.
        UOMP owns the protocol semantics; Aegis OS owns policy, leases, sandboxing, the gateway, and audit.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="container" style="margin-top:2.5rem">
      <div style="display:flex;gap:2rem;flex-wrap:wrap">

        <!-- MCP Card -->
        <div class="card" style="flex:1;min-width:320px;order:2">
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;margin-bottom:.5rem">
            <span style="font-size:2rem">🔌</span>
            <h2 style="margin:0;font-size:1.35rem">MCP Client</h2>
          </div>
          <p style="color:var(--mid);margin-bottom:.75rem;max-width:420px">
            Claude Desktop, Cursor, or any MCP client connects over stdio; <code>aegis-os memory setup</code> writes the client config, while read access is requested by the agent and approved in the local consent page.
          </p>
          <div style="background:var(--accent-soft);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:2px;padding:.75rem 1rem;margin-bottom:1.25rem;font-size:.8rem;color:var(--accent)">
            <strong>Native.</strong> <code>aegis-os memory setup claude</code> writes the bridge profile; the first tool call creates a consent request, and the local consent page opens automatically to complete approval.
          </div>
          <div style="background:var(--bg);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin-bottom:1.25rem">
            <div style="font-size:.8rem;color:var(--mid);margin-bottom:.4rem;font-weight:600">Intended workflow</div>
            <div style="font-size:.85rem;color:var(--mid);line-height:1.8">
              1. Point UOMP at an Obsidian vault with <code>aegis-os memory setup claude --vault</code><br/>
              2. Ask the client for <code>notes/projects/**</code><br/>
              3. Local consent page: select tags / keys and confirm scope; high-sensitivity items are per-key<br/>
              4. After approval the agent continues; every read is checked and logged<br/>
              5. Revoke — the next request returns <code>401 SESSION_NOT_ACTIVE</code>
            </div>
          </div>
          <a href={`${baseUrl}en/tutorial/`} style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.4rem;padding:.65rem 1.5rem;background:#233E33;border-radius:2px;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-weight:500;font-size:.9rem">
            MCP setup →
          </a>
        </div>

        <!-- CLI Card -->
        <div class="card" style="flex:1;min-width:320px;order:1;border-color:var(--accent);border-width:1px">
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;margin-bottom:.5rem">
            <span style="font-size:2rem">⌨️</span>
            <h2 style="margin:0;font-size:1.35rem">Try with the Aegis CLI</h2>
          </div>
          <p style="color:var(--mid);margin-bottom:1.25rem;max-width:400px">
            Works today. Import Obsidian/Markdown notes and grant a local agent a time-limited, revocable session.
          </p>
          <div style="background:var(--bg);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin-bottom:.75rem">
            <div style="font-size:.8rem;color:var(--mid);margin-bottom:.4rem;font-weight:600">Quick commands</div>
            <pre style="font-size:.8rem;color:var(--mid);line-height:1.75;overflow-x:auto;background:transparent;margin:0"><code>brew install aegis-os
aegis-os memory setup claude --vault ~/Obsidian/MyVault
aegis-os memory status
aegis-os memory ui
aegis-os memory pending
aegis-os memory approve &lt;request-id&gt;
aegis-os memory sessions
aegis-os memory revoke &lt;session-id&gt;</code></pre>
          </div>
          <p style="color:var(--mid);font-size:.82rem;line-height:1.6;margin-bottom:1.25rem">
            <code>setup</code> only imports notes, starts the background server, and writes the client config; it grants nothing. The first client request creates a consent request; the local consent page opens automatically (or run <code>memory ui</code>), and CLI <code>pending</code> / <code>approve</code> still works. Use <code>sessions</code> / <code>revoke</code> to revoke sessions, and <code>stop</code> to stop the server.
          </p>
          <a href={`${baseUrl}en/tutorial/`} style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.4rem;padding:.65rem 1.5rem;background:#233E33;border-radius:2px;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-weight:500;font-size:.9rem">
            CLI Tutorial →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Shared infrastructure -->
    <div class="container" style="margin-top:3.5rem">
      <div class="card" style="max-width:760px">
        <h2 style="font-size:1.15rem;margin-bottom:.75rem">Shared Infrastructure</h2>
        <p style="color:var(--mid);font-size:.88rem;line-height:1.7">
          CLI and MCP both use the Aegis OS memory module. They share the UOMP protocol, Aegis policy/leases, the Capability Token system, and audit logs. Today <code>aegis-os memory setup</code> handles one-time wiring, and the agent requests access when it needs data.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Native modules -->
    <div class="container" style="margin-top:3.5rem">
      <h2 style="font-size:1.15rem;margin-bottom:.5rem">Build on Aegis OS</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--mid);margin-bottom:1.5rem">UOMP is enforced natively by Aegis OS; Agents connect through MCP or the Aegis adapter.</p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <tr><th>Module</th><th>Responsibility</th></tr>
        <tr><td><code>aos-memory</code></td><td>scope / lease mapping, deny / field filtering, remote token policy</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>aos-memory-store</code></td><td>UOMP-compatible SQLite schema, Markdown importer, staged writes, payloads</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>aos-memory-server</code></td><td>consent requests, sessions, Ed25519 JWT, revocation, audit</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>aos-memory-gateway</code></td><td>remote Agent entry, TLS/mTLS, rate limiting, audit</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>aegis-os memory</code></td><td>user command entry (all native Rust)</td></tr>
      </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hero-btns" style="margin-top:3rem">
      <a href="https://github.com/heurion-org/aegis-os/tree/main/modules/uomp" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-h1" style="background:#233E33">UOMP module →</a>
      <a href={`${baseUrl}en/tutorial/`} class="btn-h1">Tutorial →</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/heurion-org/aegis-os" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-h2">GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
